  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "comment": "M. voltae was grown in Fe- and S-free basal medium that contained the following (in grams per liter): NaCl, 21.98; MgCl2 · 6H2O, 5.10; NaHCO3, 5.00; NH4Cl, 0.50; K2HPO4, 0.14; KCl, 0.33; and CaCl2 · 2H2O, 0.10 (Table S3)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": "All basal medium components, except NaHCO3, were dissolved in MQ H2O and then boiled for 15 min."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "After boiling, the medium was sealed with a butyl rubber stopper and sparged with N2 gas passed over a heated (200°C) and reduced copper column for 1 h per liter of medium."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "After degassing, the medium was sealed and brought into an anaerobic chamber, and NaHCO3 was added as specified above."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": "After addition of these components, the pH of the medium was adjusted to 7.00 using anoxic 2 M HCl or 1 M NaOH."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": ""
    }
  ]
}